# The failover sweep's ratchet (ADR-0055 §11): every cell of the base
# catalogue that fails today, with the decision section that owns its
# correction. A change that makes a cell pass removes its line; a new failure
# is never added without its owner. The list only shrinks.
#
# The owner is read from the finding: a second CDR where the departure sweep
# ends a call a killed primary ended behind the replication window (no marker
# tells it), §5; a request or final a copy sends without the record of what
# the dead owner sent, a request into a dialog the other copy ended, and the
# non-2xx a copy owes a caller the dead primary answered §4; a deviation no
# declared window of §11 covers, §11; a PRACK, an owed ACK or an in-dialog
# request left unanswered §2; a 2xx repeat routed through the other owner §8;
# and any other finding of a split cell §7.

refer/split/t1-applied  ADR-0055 §7  # two copies
refer/split/t2-applied  ADR-0055 §7  # two copies
refer/split/t2-left  ADR-0055 §7  # the split-off primary's setup timeout sends the caller a non-2xx after the other copy's 2xx
refer/split/t2-logged  ADR-0055 §7  # the split-off primary's setup timeout sends the caller a non-2xx after the other copy's 2xx
reinvite/primary-killed/t6-logged  ADR-0055 §11  # the test callee never retransmits its re-INVITE 2xx (RFC 3261 §13.3.1.4): the 2xx the dead primary took never reaches the copy, which 487s the caller's re-INVITE at her BYE and she leaves it unACKed
reinvite/split-healed/t5-left  ADR-0055 §7  # two copies
reinvite/split-healed/t5-logged  ADR-0055 §7  # two copies
reinvite/split/t1-applied  ADR-0055 §7  # two copies
reinvite/split/t2-applied  ADR-0055 §7  # two copies
reinvite/split/t2-left  ADR-0055 §7  # the split-off primary's setup timeout sends the caller a non-2xx after the other copy's 2xx
reinvite/split/t2-logged  ADR-0055 §7  # the split-off primary's setup timeout sends the caller a non-2xx after the other copy's 2xx
reinvite/split/t5-applied  ADR-0055 §7  # second copy acts on an ended dialog
reinvite/split/t5-left  ADR-0055 §7  # second copy acts on an ended dialog
reinvite/split/t5-logged  ADR-0055 §7  # second copy acts on an ended dialog
